1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,952
"Just a 5-minute quick call, Kabir?" 8:47 pm. Third time this week.

2
00:00:05,952 --> 00:00:11,250
His dinner's going cold. He types "Sure sir." And stops.

3
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:15,846
Option A: yes, again. Every night becomes office.

4
00:00:15,846 --> 00:00:21,465
Option B: a flat no. True, but it can sour things.

5
00:00:21,465 --> 00:00:26,329
The third road? William Ury calls it the positive no.

6
00:00:26,329 --> 00:00:33,082
First, a Yes! to yourself: what are you protecting? Family dinner. A fresh mind.

7
00:00:33,082 --> 00:00:37,912
Then a No. Clear and calm, no long excuses: "I can't take a call right now."

8
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:44,930
Then a Yes? A proposal: "10 am tomorrow, first thing? Send the agenda."

9
00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:49,769
Riya smiles. Like last episode, there's often an Option C.

10
00:00:49,769 --> 00:00:52,616
Send this to the colleague who never says no.

11
00:00:52,616 --> 00:00:56,008
Remember: put your No between two yeses.

12
00:00:56,008 --> 00:01:02,471
Would you take the 8:47 call, or say "10 am, first thing"? 1 or 2?
